{:source-commit "3ba572c553b1a45627e5abe4927fd42784b12d2f", :patterns [["carrying" "Carrying capacity"] ["distributed_roadmap" "Emergent Roadmap"] ["heartbeat" "Heartbeat"] ["newcomer" "Newcomer"] ["pattern_audit" "Pattern Audit Routine"] ["peeragogy" "Peeragogy"] ["reduce" "Reduce, reuse, recycle"] ["roadmap" "Roadmap"] ["scrapbook" "Scrapbook"] ["specific" "A specific project"] ["wrapper" "Wrapper"]], :edges ({:from "carrying", :to "roadmap", :from-title "Carrying capacity", :to-title "Roadmap", :section "Solution                                                             :key:", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "Use the project [[file:roadmap.org][Roadmap]] to make note of obstacles."} {:from "heartbeat", :to "carrying", :from-title "Heartbeat", :to-title "Carrying capacity", :section "Rationale", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…an quick way to do a reality check and find the project's strongest pulse: the activities that sustain a healthy project should sustain us, too (cf. [[file:pattern-carrying.org][Carrying capacity]]).…"} {:from "heartbeat", :to "scrapbook", :from-title "Heartbeat", :to-title "Scrapbook", :section "Resolution", :whats-next? false, :sign :negative, :quote "…On the other hand, if a specific activity is no longer sustaining the project, stop doing it, much as you would move an out-of-date pattern to the [[file:scrapbook.org][Scrapbook]] in order to make room for other concerns. The power of the Heartbeat is that the project can be as focused and intensive as it needs to…"} {:from "newcomer", :to "reduce", :from-title "Newcomer", :to-title "Reduce, reuse, recycle", :section "Problem", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…of ideas that the old-timers have never considered -- or they may think they have new ideas, which are actually a different take on an old idea; see [[file:reduce_reuse_recycle.org][Reduce, reuse, recycle]]. People who are new to the project can tell you what makes their participation difficult. Since you're learning…"} {:from "newcomer", :to "scrapbook", :from-title "Newcomer", :to-title "Scrapbook", :section "Solution", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…with particular emphasis on educational applications, is surveyed in [5]. One method for doing the reflection/assessment step is presented in the [[file:scrapbook.org][Scrapbook]] pattern. Be flexible: networked attention (even more so than rigid cycles [3]) leads to new ways of knowing and expanded access to…"} {:from "peeragogy", :to "specific", :from-title "Peeragogy", :to-title "A specific project", :section "Solution", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…in interconnected networks that may reach all over the world. Importantly, while people involved in a peeragogical process may be collaborating on [[file:a_specific_project.org][A specific project]], they don't have to be direct collaborators outside of the learning context or co-located in time or space. Just as…"} {:from "roadmap", :to "heartbeat", :from-title "Roadmap", :to-title "Heartbeat", :section "Rationale", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…was a \"crowdsourced\" outline of the first edition of the /Peeragogy Handbook/. Later, it took the form of a schedule of meetings following a regular [[file:heartbeat.org][Heartbeat]], supplemented by a list of upcoming deadlines. Most recently, our roadmap is expressed in the emergent objectives collected at the end…"} {:from "roadmap", :to "newcomer", :from-title "Roadmap", :to-title "Newcomer", :section "Solution", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…Building a guide to the goals, activities, experiments and working methods can help [[file:newcomer.org][Newcomers]] and old-timers alike understand their relationship with the project. It may combine features of a manifesto, a syllabus, and an issue…"} {:from "roadmap", :to "wrapper", :from-title "Roadmap", :to-title "Wrapper", :section "Solution", :whats-next? false, :sign :positive, :quote "…from /here/ to